      "side": 1,
      "message": "It passes emdawnwebgpu_tests_asyncify. ValidateCallbackMode doesn\u0027t fail on when we default-init, as it allows `mode\u003d\u003d0` if `callback\u003d\u003dnullptr`. I think this is effectively the same as what Dawn does in release builds.\n\nFor reference:\nin Dawn we also default the device descriptor to the default struct:\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/Adapter.cpp;l\u003d390;drc\u003dede56a97b66cd6305865582b0b0d5336db71682c\nbut for the DeviceLost callback we default to either AllowSpontaneous + a debug printer, or AllowProcessEvents + nullptr:\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/Device.cpp;l\u003d190;drc\u003d02446d66622a0a811448be7bb4ac8939c5b00aa9",
